        "original_id": "74d9d472-751d-528e-9d10-7a60d3f7f354",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Howard Bilerman, Vic Chesnutt, Basia Bulat\n- Bands: Arcade Fire, Thee Silver Mt. Zion Memorial Orchestra & Tra-La-La Band\n- Albums: Funeral, Oh, My Darling\n- Places: Montreal, Athens, Georgia\n- Roles: drummer, producer, singer-songwriter\n\nFacts:\n- James Victor Chesnutt was born on November 12, 1964, and was an American singer-songwriter from Athens, Georgia.\n- Basia Bulat met Howard Bilerman in 2006 and later asked him to work with her on the album Oh, My Darling.\n- Howard Bilerman was a former member of Arcade Fire and recorded and played drums on the band's debut album Funeral.\n- Howard Bilerman also recorded on releases by Thee Silver Mt. Zion Memorial Orchestra & Tra-La-La Band, Vic Chesnutt, Basia Bulat, Peter Peter, Rich Aucoin, and Angela Desveaux.\n- Oh, My Darling was recorded in Montreal and produced by Howard Bilerman.\n- James Victor Chesnutt died on December 25, 2009.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
